      "writtenOn": "2026-04-28T12:51:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wrt to `checked_cast`, if you want to rely on the compiler to optimize out the check, I suppose we could do that; but I trust the compiler less in this case because it wants to optimize less around aborts (checks). If we keep the code I added, we should beef up the testing for `checked_cast`.\n\nWrt to two checks (checked_cast + hardening), I feel like we shouldn\u0027t do the hardening ourselves, because then there\u0027s a difference beyond strong typing between the `ityp` containers and regular containers. OOB access in containers is an understood problem, and there\u0027s enough hardening in standard libraries that I don\u0027t think we need to do it ourselves.",
      "parentUuid": "ebfb6be1_d54d513e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 106,
        "endChar": 35
