      "writtenOn": "2026-04-28T13:26:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both fair points.\n\nI think it is OK to rely on optimizations for casts that don\u0027t require checks. It should be pretty straightforward. I tested and Clang was able to optimize this.\n\nUnfortunately Clang was NOT able to combine the two checks (checked_cast + hardening check). But I think this is fine because it ONLY matters for 64-bit index types on 32-bit builds.\n\nResults here: https://godbolt.org/z/6b7hvcdch\n\nRevision incoming.",
